projects.description:
Selected and implemented 5 popular role mining algorithms (ORCA, GO, HPr, HPe, HM);
Crawled 222,734 <app, permission> tuples from Android Market (covering 44,971 applications) as dataset;
Conducted role mining and analyzed the feasibility of enforcing RBAC on Android platform;
Mined semantic meaning for each role using TF-IDF.

The system is aimed at tracing and recording the lifecycle of agriculture products;
I was involved in prototype implementation; My work included implement the prototype system runable on single machine using SSH framework; mainly focusing on Hibernate part.

Publication: W. Han, Y. Gu, W. Wang, Y. Zhang, Y. Yin, J. Wang, L. Zheng, “The Design of an Electronic Pedigree System for Food Safety”, Information Systems Frontiers (ISF), August 2012, (DOI: 10.1007/s10796-012-9372-7), accepted.

